Third-party libraries in the Monadic Chat AppImage
==================================================

The AppImage carries six shared libraries in usr/lib, added by the AppImage
build tooling (electron-builder). They are unmodified copies of files from
Ubuntu 18.04 (bionic) packages:

  Library                     Ubuntu package and version                        License
  libXss.so.1.0.0             libxss1 1:1.2.2-1                                 MIT/X11
  libXtst.so.6.1.0            libxtst6 2:1.2.3-1                                MIT/X11
  libnotify.so.4.0.0          libnotify4 0.7.7-3ubuntu0.18.04.1                 LGPL-2.1
  libgconf-2.so.4.1.5         libgconf-2-4 3.2.6-4ubuntu1                       LGPL-2
  libappindicator3.so.1.0.0   libappindicator3-1 12.10.1+18.04.20200408.1-0ubuntu1
                                                                                GPL-3 (some files LGPL-2.1)
  libindicator3.so.7.0.0      libindicator3-7 16.10.0+18.04.20180321.1-0ubuntu1 GPL-3

Copyright notices and license terms
-----------------------------------

Each package's copyright file is in usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright.
The license texts they refer to are in usr/share/common-licenses
(GPL-3, LGPL-2, LGPL-2.1).

Corresponding source
--------------------

The complete source of each library is its Ubuntu source package
(original source, Ubuntu changes and .dsc file):

  libxss           1:1.2.2-1
  libxtst          2:1.2.3-1
  libnotify        0.7.7-3ubuntu0.18.04.1
  gconf            3.2.6-4ubuntu1
  libappindicator  12.10.1+18.04.20200408.1-0ubuntu1
  libindicator     16.10.0+18.04.20180321.1-0ubuntu1

These source packages are attached to every Monadic Chat release on GitHub
that includes an AppImage, as monadic-chat_<version>_linux-library-sources.tar,
together with a SHA256SUMS file:

  https://github.com/yohasebe/monadic-chat/releases

They are also available from the Ubuntu archive
(http://archive.ubuntu.com/ubuntu/pool/, or
http://old-releases.ubuntu.com/ubuntu/pool/ once Ubuntu 18.04 moves there).

